<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Charm Animal</h1>
<p>Sphere: Mind Sphere
Class: Druid (guild level 15), Ranger (guild level 25, up to 60%)
Mana: 20
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cast charm animal &lt;animal&gt;
tell &lt;animal&gt; &lt;command&gt;
</pre>
<p>The caster utters 'Voce sequi', and a wild animal is tamed: it wakes, 
stands and follows the caster, and does what it is told. Command it with 
tell, for example tell wolf kill rat. It fights, walks and does most 
things you ask, but it won't talk, cast, steal, use or recite things, and 
it won't attack another player unless both of you have signed the Book of 
Blood.
</p><p>It only works on animals; the animal resists with its mind, and animals of 
a higher level than you are harder to charm. If the spell fails, the 
animal growls and attacks you. You can have only one animal in your 
service at a time.
</p><p>The charm doesn't last: after a short while the animal longs for its 
natural habitat, and it goes back there. A dispel magic strong enough ends 
it at once. You must be standing. It is also found on scrolls.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
